LRC neighbor/tournament lift (codex-2026-05-31 S431)
All times and distances are exact Fractions inherited from S356.

LRC TOURNAMENT-LIFT METHODOLOGY
================================================================================================
lens                               data                                   tournament use
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
scalar lonely gap                  min_i ||v_i t||                        height of a lower envelope
                                                                          too lossy: forgets all pairwise runner relations
danger rank tournament             orient i->j if i is closer to 0 than j momentary threat order
                                                                          transitive, useful mostly as a braid/order-change trace
circular half-distance tournament  i->j if j is clockwise within 1/2 from i round/incomplete tournament from positions
                                                                          sees antipodal ties, SCCs, and circular order strata
two-nearest graph                  each runner points to its two nearest neighbors local contact graph
                                                                          possible LRC analogue of tournament good-cut cores
pairwise distance ledger           all ||(v_i-v_j)t||                     difference-speed LRC shadow
                                                                          detects quotient collisions invisible to zero-distance scalar
residue quotient tournament        positions at t=p/q are v_i p mod q     labelled cyclic tournament with multiplicities
                                                                          tight examples often collapse to small residue polygons

